# measurement-real-siblings.out
#
# THE TWO LINES FROM THE REPORTING LOOP, RUN AGAINST THE REAL ARTIFACTS.
#
# measurement-provenance-consumer.out proves the verifier CAN fail, on images
# this repository built for the purpose. This file shows the same two lines as
# they actually appear in `publish_siblings`, run against the sibling images
# the e2e tier really pulls.
#
# repo:   /Users/kaka/Code/any/moon/cafaye/wt-m39-provenance-parlor
# commit: 11d6c5b
# run:    2026-10-03T03:27:52Z
#
# WHAT IS AND IS NOT CLAIMED. This is not a run of `./bin/e2e-stack
# publish-siblings` — that rebuilds and republishes both siblings and takes
# minutes. These are the loop's own two command lines, verbatim, against
# the images that run would report on. What it shows is the verifier being
# consulted on real pulled images, and both failure shapes occurring for real.
#
#   identity  -> exit 4, "carries no labels at all". The trap the stamp
#                handoff names, on the image it names.
#   guard     -> exit 0, and a confident FALSE answer: source and revision
#                are oven/bun's, inherited through FROM. --verify cannot
#                tell an inherited stamp from its own.
#
# Two different digests on the two lines above, which is the whole reason the
# digest line was KEPT: the stamp did not and could not produce either of
# them.
#
================================================================================
--- the reporting loop's own two lines, against cafaye/identity:e2e
$ docker image inspect --format '{{index .RepoDigests 0}}' cafaye/identity:e2e
localhost:16004/cafaye/identity@sha256:6f811e1277181789702d9520252bff74fee59a048b1290bf81d1d0af533bcc57
$ sh "$ROOT/docker/provenance.sh" --verify cafaye/identity:e2e || true
kit-provenance: cafaye/identity:e2e carries no labels at all — it was built without the stamp.
kit-provenance:   (kit: docker/Dockerfile.<lang> declares the ARGs and the LABELs; this image predates it, or was built elsewhere.)
[loop continues: exit of the whole '|| true' form is 0]

--- the reporting loop's own two lines, against cafaye/guard:e2e
